#project("Most Efficient Portfolio | Canadian Home Bias", url: "https://github.com/faketut/course/tree/main/cfm301/projects/cfm301-project1-efficient-portfolio")
- Built a CAD-denominated mean-variance frontier from five regional equity ETFs over *275 months*; quadratic programs and a γ = 3 utility criterion put the optimal Canadian weight at *48%*, close to the *\~50%* observed home bias versus Canada's *\~3%* global market cap.
- Ran sensitivity across γ = 1–10 and the minimum-variance criterion, documenting corner solutions and error maximization.
